page DocsProviderMachines

title "Machines - Documentation"

template
<div class="min-h-[calc(100vh-4rem)] grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] bg-page transition-colors">

  <DocsSidebar active="provider-machines" />

  <div class="min-w-0 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-10 py-6 sm:py-10">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">

    <article class="rounded-3xl border border-line bg-panel p-5 sm:p-8">
      <p class="text-zinc-500 text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-3">Documentation / Cloud providers</p>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-light uppercase tracking-wide text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">Machines</h1>
      <p class="text-zinc-500 text-sm mt-2 mb-8">Every server in the provider account, including ones the deployer did not create, with power controls.</p>

      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">If your Tylix Deploy subscription needs payment, the page turns view only. Buttons that change something are greyed out and read &ldquo;Pay to continue&rdquo;. You can still look at everything.</p>
      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">The list</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">The top shows how many machines there are, how many are running and how many are offline. Type in the search box to filter by name or IP. Select <strong>Refresh</strong> to read the account again.</p>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">Each row shows the name, the IP, a status, the region, the plan and the creation date. A machine whose IP matches one of your servers links to that server's page. One that does not shows <strong>Not added to deployer</strong>.</p>
      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Power controls</h2>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden mb-8">
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Boot</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Shown on an offline machine.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Reboot</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Shown on a running machine. Asks &ldquo;Reboot name?&rdquo; first.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Shut down</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Shown on a running machine. Asks &ldquo;Shut name down?&rdquo; first. Sites on it go offline.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-8">Select the button, then <strong>Yes, do it</strong>. The row says &ldquo;Working&hellip; this page updates itself&rdquo; and the list is re-read every few seconds until the machine settles. While a machine is starting, rebooting or stopping, the buttons are replaced by &ldquo;Wait for it to finish before sending another action.&rdquo;</p>
      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Statuses</h2>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden mb-8">
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Running</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Up and answering.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Offline</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Switched off. You can boot it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Starting, Rebooting, Stopping</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Changing state. Wait.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Migrating, Rebuilding, Deleting</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">The provider is working on it. Wait.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">If something goes wrong</h2>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden mb-8">
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Couldn't load machines. Try again.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">The provider did not answer. Select Refresh.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Couldn't send that to the provider. Try again.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">The power action was refused. The provider's reason is shown when it gives one.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">No machines in this account</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Nothing exists at the provider yet. Create a server and it appears here.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">If the API token is missing a permission this page needs, a message at the top says which one and how to fix it. Add the permission to the token at the provider, then reload.</p>

      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 mt-8 pt-5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
        <a href="/docs/providers/overview" class="text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">&larr; Provider overview</a>
        <a href="/docs/providers/firewalls" class="text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">Firewalls &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

  </div>
  </div>
</div>
